    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d3">

                <pb facs="0096" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890b.6363 Gulf Oil Corporation/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-02T13:00:00-05:00">February 2, 1932—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>50. Your despatch 2482, December 29, 1931. If you have not received the reply
                    promised by Oliphant please take up the
                    matter again informally with the Foreign Office. Explain that the Department
                    does not wish to be unduly insistent in this matter, but since the whole
                    question has been under consideration by the interested departments of the
                    British Government for some time it is hoped that a reply may soon be
                    received.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
